.TH SINDOOK 1 "2026-08-27" "sindook 0.10.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
sindook \- seal and open files with hybrid post-quantum encryption
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sindook
.I command
.RI [ flags "] [" FILE ...]
.br
.B sindook version
.br
.B sindook help
.RI [ command ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Sindook encrypts files for X-Wing recipients (X25519 + ML-KEM-768),
a passphrase, or both, and can rotate access without decrypting or
re-encrypting the payload in fast mode. Each sealed file carries key
slots following the LUKS model; any one slot opens the file.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B keygen
create an identity, optionally passphrase-protected
.TP
.B init
create or select the explicit default identity
.TP
.B pubkey
print the public key of an identity
.TP
.B contacts
save and use named recipient public keys and groups
.TP
.B config
inspect and change saved settings (default identity)
.TP
.B paths
show the portable Sindook configuration locations
.TP
.B seal
encrypt to recipients and/or a passphrase
.TP
.B open
decrypt with an identity or passphrase
.TP
.B verify
confirm sealed files decrypt cleanly, writing nothing
.TP
.B inspect
show sealed-file metadata, no credentials needed
.TP
.B rewrap
rotate recipients, passphrases, or the file key
.TP
.B shred
overwrite files before deleting them
.TP
.B selftest
run the built-in cryptographic self tests
.TP
.B doctor
diagnose the installation and optionally check for updates
.TP
.B completion
print a bash, zsh, fish, or powershell completion script
.TP
.B version
print version and build provenance
.PP
Run
.B sindook help
.I command
for flags and examples. Flags may appear before or after file
operands; a literal filename beginning with \fB\-\fP follows
.BR \-\- .
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
success
.TP
.B 1
command failure (I/O error, malformed input, validation)
.TP
.B 2
command-selection or flag-parsing usage error
.TP
.B 3
authentication failure (wrong identity or passphrase, missing
credential, or header tampering)
.SH SECURITY
Sindook is pre-1.0 and has not received an independent security audit.
It is not FIPS validated and does not claim to be quantum-proof. The
X-Wing KEM is an Internet-Draft whose security depends on the draft's
model. Read the threat model, security model, and security policy in
the repository documentation before protecting sensitive data.
